 "result": "It's a Flask-style layout, renamed to `tessel`.\n\n- **`src/tessel/sessions.py`**\n  - `SignedCookieSessionInterface` is the default session interface. Its `serializer` attribute is `session_json_serializer`, an instance of `TypedCookieSerializer`. It passes that serializer to the signing serializer (line ~316), so the cookie payload goes through it.\n  - `SignedCookieSession` is the session object (a `CallbackDict` plus `SessionMixin`).\n- **`src/tessel/json/tag.py`**\n  - `TypedCookieSerializer` holds an ordered list of tag classes. `tag()` converts a value to JSON-safe form, and `untag()` reverses it using the key marker.\n  - `TypeMarker` is the base tagger class. Each subclass checks a value's type, converts it to JSON, and converts it back.\n  - The relevant taggers:\n    - `TagTuple` stores tuples as lists and restores them as tuples.\n    - `TagBytes` stores bytes as base64 text.\n    - `TagDateTime` stores datetimes as HTTP date strings.\n  - Supporting taggers: `TagDict` escapes dicts that would collide with a tag key, `PassDict` and `PassList` recurse into plain containers, and `TagMarkup` and `TagUUID` handle those types.\n\nOn load, the serializer sees a one-key dict whose key is a tag marker and routes it to that tagger's `to_python`, which restores the original type.",
